The initial triage already exposes an important distinction: the paper proves hardness only for an online algorithm class on two independent \(G(n,1/2)\) graphs, while also giving an \(O(n^2\log n)\) greedy algorithm up to the \(2\log_2 n\) threshold. I’m now reading the exact definitions and proofs to see whether a planted offline witness would preserve the paper’s distribution and theorem regime—it likely does not.
